A||||5||batboy||the Batmobile rides again||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||10-07-2000||08:10 PM||||I was mad at the Batmobile. It had broke down like a widow at a funeral. I couldn't figure out what was wrong, why it was sick. It fought me and stubbornly refused to let me repair it. I gave up in disgust and went about my business. I'd come home from work and snarl at the parked Batmobile as I walked by it. It would give me a nasty growl back and then go back to oozing oil onto the driveway again.<P>Finally, I started looking at other cars. At first, the Batmobile wasn't worried. I was only checking out second-hand four-doors. The Batmobile got a little nervious when I began looking at low-mileage Grand Prix GT coupes. Then it began sweating and became scared when I began lusting after a new 2000 Grand Prix limited edition Daytona 500 pace car. See the listed link for more of that story.<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/000760.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/000760.html</A> <P>Suddenly, the Batmobile's attitude dramatically changed. It let me finally locate exactly where the oil leak was. It let me carefully loosen the pan (without removing the bolts all the way) and to squeeze some RTV around the crack in the gasket. Oh boy! It worked! The leak stopped. Yippee!<P>BUT... in the process of test driving and checking for leaks, I found out the battery was not keeping a charge. After farting with that for a while, I finally figured out it was a bad battery. Slapped in an extra one I had handy and we were in business. The ralley gauge pod had came loose, but it turned out to be a quick and easy fix.<P>All systems go! I decided to drive the Batmobile on a long test drive to Topeka for a little Wal-Mart shopping, maybe to look at new a couple newcars, and last but not least, a hearty dinner.<P>The guys at the Pontiac Dealership got a kick out of looking over the Batmobile. They made a big fuss out of it having a V8. The Batmobile had to show off when we were leaving by burning a little rubber going out the car lot's driveway.<P>I looked at the Daytona pace car again and drove it again (see above link for full story). After chowing down on some vittles, we headed home via the long way. The Batmobile was purring at 60 MPH like a contented cheetah when suddenly an Acura buzzed up behind me and wanted to play some highway tag. I had to smoke him about three times before he gave up.<P>Then a newish black Mustang GT showed up to play. I had the sunroof cracked open with the CD player cranking out Pink Floyd's "Money" as I blew the Rustang 5 point slow away. What a nice cruise. I'm glad the Batmobile and I kissed and made up again. Maybe I don't need that Daytona 500 pace car after all.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||10-07-2000||08:32 PM||||Oh yeah, I almost forgot. I stopped for gas at a Casey's and a guy I sort of knew was working the counter. It seems he's back in school working on his master's and this is his weekend job. I bought the used 1988 Z-28 roller 350 short block from this guy that I rebuilt and am planning on using in the Batmobile. After chatting about hotrods for a while, he mentioned being broke and being willing to sell more hipo parts for cash. Well, well, well... seems he's willing to part with a nice pair of Corvette aluminum heads, completely checked out, rebuilt, and ready to go, with the machine shop ticket to prove everything was done right. They have new guides and have been machined for the bigger valve springs. The heads have all new stainless steel Manly valves and screw-in rocker studs were installed. For a mere $350 I can own this pair of heads. He has much more tied up in them than that, obviously. I've been looking for this deal on aluminum heads for over a year now. Wow! Maybe my luck is finally changing. Maybe a Hooter's (registered trademark) waitress will ask me out on a date soon.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-07-2000||09:39 PM||||Glad to hear your ride is back in service.<BR>Hmmmm, a Hooter's waitress in a Fiero....does it get any better than that?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
